  "BEST_WHY": "The light is a tile-resolution occlusion mask, not a radial blob, and it is the only thing in the deck that shows real technical craft. Isolating the added layer (4 minus 2) shows a hard, stair-stepped silhouette that steps in ~27px increments \u2014 the wall stub at x\u2248500,y\u2248390 throws a wedge of shadow down-right, and the corridor at x\u2248505\u2013540 is lit as a narrow strip up to y\u2248250 while the wall faces flanking it stay dark. Light is being blocked by geometry, then blurred at the boundary, rather than pasted over it. Second, the intensity is placed just short of clipping: in the pool core (330,430)\u2013(500,560) only 2.2% of red-channel pixels sit at 255, identical to the dimmest variant, while the core mean rises from 190.6 to 204.1. The result is a pool that reads as carried without erasing anything \u2014 the salmon mortar grid between the slabs at x\u2248448, 470, 496, 524, 550 survives intact right through the brightest part.",
