  "FLAGGED": "1, 3\n\n3 is flagged despite ranking third: in the pool core, 49.5% of red-channel pixels are pinned at 255 and 11.2% of green with it. Across roughly 20,000 pixels the image clips to a flat cream plateau \u2014 16,602 pixels sit at \u2265250 against 754 in image 2. At 5\u00d7 on the crop (300,440)\u2013(430,540) the slab mortar grid that is plainly visible in 2 and 4 is **gone**, replaced by mushy blotches, and the hue slides toward yellow-white where red saturates and green doesn't. That is the \"a filter was run over it\" read, and it is visible at thumbnail size.",
